  "conclusion": "Original A-0, standalone B-0 and decoded B-0 are byte-identical and match the committed manifest. Both scratch conversions and presentation variants have identical opaque RGBA rasters. Local view-image calls displayed originals and metadata-stripped/reserialized variants correctly while displaying scratch files black. A fresh follow-up inconsistently reported original A-0 visible but byte-identical original B-0 and the reserialization black. Thus the exact presentation mechanism is not established and metadata removal is not a proven reliable fix. No source/image-selection/movie defect or original artifact replacement is supported.",
